A linear electric fireplace is a horizontally elongated heating unit that can be recessed into a wall or mounted on a surface. It uses high‑definition LED or 3D‑flame technology to create a continuous, realistic flame effect while delivering heat through an efficient electric heating element. Prices typically start around $800–$1 500 for basic models and can climb to $6 000–$10 000 for extra‑long, fully customized installations that span entire feature walls.
